    "summary": "Baluchi-style woman&#039;s baggy trousers (sirwal) made of turquoise-green satin silk; part of a three-piece outfit. The trousers have an elasticated waist and wide ankles that cover the heels when worn. The trouser-cuffs are worked in similar box-stitched hand-embroidery as the matching dress (dishdasha or pashk, 2011,6003.44a) and head-shawl (shadar) (2011,6003.44c), with colourful bands, diamond-shapes and snowflake patterns reaching calf-height.",
